{
  "__comment": "The parts of the grid that turn: the rear shaft standing in the gearbox well, and the cogwheel in the gap. Drawn by the block entity's Flywheel visual, not by the chunk mesh - a visual does not suppress the block model, so anything here must be absent from block/p_grid or it renders twice, once spinning and once still. Authored pointing south (+Z), because OrientedRotatingVisual.backHorizontal turns SOUTH onto the block's facing.getOpposite(), which is the face the shaft is on. The cogwheel is Create's cogwheel_shaftless stood on the Z axis, teeth and all: they reach past the block, out through the window in the rims, which is how it meshes with a neighbouring cogwheel the way Create's own crafter does. No texture_size, and no uv rescaled to suit one: the string 'texture_size' does not appear anywhere in NeoForge or Minecraft, so it is a Blockbench authoring note the game ignores. Every uv here is normalised by 16 whatever the texture's real resolution. Doubling the axis uvs to 'match' a 32x32 atlas ran them past the edge of the sprite and the shaft rendered black.",
